# Who owns what, for the paths where a change means a change to the rules.
#
# The organisation has no teams, so owners are individuals. Four accounts hold admin on this
# repository: @RamzesX, @filip-plata, @jakubs21, @pZmudzki.
#
# Today this file documents ownership rather than enforcing it: the ruleset on main requires a
# pull request and a green `Merge verdict`, but zero approvals, because GitHub does not let an
# author approve their own pull request and this repository has one maintainer. Requiring an
# approval with no bypass would make every pull request unmergeable. The moment a second person
# has write access, raising that count to 1 turns every line below into a hard gate with no other
# change needed. See docs/ci/GOVERNING-MACHINE-WRITTEN-CHANGE.md §9.

*                                   @RamzesX

# ── The invariant surfaces ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An agent may propose any of these and ratify none of them.

# Ratchets and budgets: lowering is free, raising is a governance event.
